<title>USA: PSE&amp;G 1,031 MW NJ nuke back to full output.</title>
<headline>PSE&amp;G 1,031 MW NJ nuke back to full output.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-11-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Public Service Enterprise Group Inc (PSE&amp;G) said Monday its 1,031 megawatt (MW) Hope Creek nuclear generating station reached full output Sunday following a brief maintenance outage.</p>
<p>The plant in Salem, N.J., was shut November 2 to repair its valves in the reactor's recirculating system.</p>
<p>Public Service Enterprise is the operator and majority owner of the Hope Creek facility.</p>
<p>--New York Power Desk +1 212 859 1622</p>
